From: Project Luma <luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: eswin_eph861x: reset the controller before unmasking its interrupt

With eswin,suspend-mode = <2> (EPH_SUSPEND_REGULATOR) on SPI, eph_stop()
only calls disable_irq(): the regulators stay on and the controller keeps
running for the whole suspend with nobody reading its reports. eph_start()
then only calls enable_irq(). On the Fairphone 6 no further interrupts
arrive after a system resume.

The vendor driver has no dev_pm_ops. Its panel-notifier wake path
(eph_dev_enter_normal_mode) pulses the reset line before enable_irq() on
every wake. Do the same in eph_start(), which eph_resume() and input open
both reach while the interrupt is still masked, and log the CHG level
after the reset.
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/eswin_touch/eswin_eph861x.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/eswin_touch/eswin_eph861x.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/eswin_touch/eswin_eph861x.c
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/eswin_touch/eswin_eph861x.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/eswin_touch/eswin_eph861x.c
@@ -1464,6 +1464,15 @@ static int eph_start(struct eph_data *ephdata)
     switch (ephdata->ephplatform->suspend_mode)
     {
         case EPH_SUSPEND_REGULATOR:
+            #if (ESWIN_EPH861X_SPI)
+            /*
+             * eph_stop() only masked the interrupt: the controller kept
+             * running and may hold a report nobody read. Reset it before
+             * unmasking, as the vendor wake path does.
+             */
+            eph_reset_device(ephdata);
+            dev_info(&commsdevice->dev, "%s, reset done, chg %d\n", __func__, eph_read_chg(ephdata));
+            #endif
             enable_irq(ephdata->chg_irq);
             #if (ESWIN_EPH861X_I2C)
             /* TODO Pixel4XL specific - Temporary comment out diabling/enable of regulator due to demo handset specific issues */
